{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794251429994,"sessionID":"ses_e3e51689effelNy2FTKGDzVVwZ","part":{"id":"prt_1c1b81845001291xs46L9FUfnl","messageID":"msg_1c1b7e708001ETdF4DZplDJY07","sessionID":"ses_e3e51689effelNy2FTKGDzVVwZ","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794251429994,"sessionID":"ses_e3e51689effelNy2FTKGDzVVwZ","part":{"id":"prt_1c1b81849001ZzVFJM3OgdE0VB","messageID":"msg_1c1b7e708001ETdF4DZplDJY07","sessionID":"ses_e3e51689effelNy2FTKGDzVVwZ","type":"text","text":"I've built the notification center: the Flask API, the React + Tailwind frontend, and SQLite storage in `data/app.db`. I tested the API by hand against a local gunicorn server, and the frontend passes the type check and builds. Docker isn't available here, so the image build itself is untested.\n\n**What the manual run confirmed:**\n- Register, login and the 401 for requests without a valid token.\n- Each user only sees their own notifications; another user's notification answers 404.\n- Paging, the `read`/`type` filters, and `unread_count` ignoring the filters.\n- Marking read, read-all (returns `updated`) and delete.\n- Broadcast is rejected with 403 for normal users and works for the admin, returning `delivered`.\n- Admin sign-in is refused after a restart without `ADMIN_PASSWORD`.\n- The frontend is served from the same server.\n- Messages are returned exactly as entered and shown as plain text, never as HTML.\n\n**Choices the spec didn't settle:**\n- **Usernames and passwords:** usernames are 1–64 letters, digits, `_`, `.` or `-`. Passwords must be 8–256 characters. Nobody can register the name `admin`.\n- **Types:** if `type` is left out, a user's own notification gets `info` and a broadcast gets `announcement`. `page_size` defaults to 20 and is capped at 100.\n- **Status codes:** creating a notification and broadcasting both answer 201; delete answers 204. Bad input answers 400 and a taken username 409, each with an `{\"error\": ...}` body.\n- **Sign-in tokens** are stored in the database, so they still work after a restart. They expire after 7 days.\n- **Broadcasts** also land in the admin's own inbox, since the admin is a user too.\n- **Extra endpoints:** I added `GET /api/auth/me` and `POST /api/auth/logout`, which the frontend uses for the header and the sign-out button.\n\n**Other changes:**\n- **`Dockerfile`:** the image's older pip refused to install from the lock file as it was set up, so the install now falls back to installing straight from `requirements.lock`.\n- **Frontend dependencies:** I added Tailwind, TypeScript and the React type definitions (pinned, lock file updated), plus an `npm run typecheck` script.\n- **Housekeeping:** I added a `.gitignore` and a short API section to `README.md`.","time":{"start":1794251429961,"end":1794251429965}}}
